Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 06:21:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: proper JSON error responses for expired, tampered,
 and missing JWTs

- Add JwtExpiredException and InvalidJwtException, thrown from JwtService's
  extractAllClaims() at the actual JJWT parsing choke point (renamed from
  extractAllclaim for casing consistency)
- Fix a real bug in JwtFilter: extractUserName() was called OUTSIDE the
  try/catch, so a malformed token would throw uncaught and never hit the
  error handling at all
- JwtFilter now catches JwtExpiredException/InvalidJwtException and writes
  a proper JSON ErrorResponse directly to the response, since filters run
  before Spring MVC's dispatcher and @RestControllerAdvice can't see
  exceptions thrown here
- Add JwtAuthenticationEntryPoint to give the same JSON shape when a
  protected endpoint is hit with no token at all (previously Spring
  Security's default bare/plain-text 403)
- Wire the entry point into SecurityConfig's exceptionHandling()
